  "result": "Webhook deliveries to a customer's endpoint are retried by `src/server/jobs/webhook-delivery-job.ts`. It sets both the attempt limit and the wait growth.\n\n- **Attempts allowed:** `MAX_ATTEMPTS = 6` in that file. `runWebhookDeliveryJob` marks a delivery failed for good with \"giving up after N attempts\" once `delivery.attempts > MAX_ATTEMPTS`. That is how the oldest queued messages get dropped.\n- **Wait growth:** `backoffMs(attempts)` doubles the wait each time. It gives 1s, 2s, 4s and so on, capped at 300,000 ms (five minutes). Attempt 0 retries immediately.\n\nTwo other places look similar but are not the answer:\n- `WEBHOOK_MAX_ATTEMPTS = 5` in `src/config/constants.ts` is not referenced by any code. The job uses its own local constant of 6.\n- `src/server/jobs/queue.ts` is a separate generic job queue with its own limit of 5 attempts and a 60-second cap. It doesn't handle webhook deliveries.\n\nANSWER: src/server/jobs/webhook-delivery-job.ts",
